C-PHY: the three-phase mode goes in the common block, BEFORE the trios

Measured with r132 (patch 0090 already in):

    csiphy0: link_freq=435200000 settle_cnt=21 lane_mask=0x07 num_data=3 ctrl5=0x2a
    packets = 0
    CONTROL front camera in the same session = 3054 packets

So the 0x2a did reach the hardware -it is the exact value the vendor computes
for three trios- and it is not enough.

WHAT WAS STILL WRONG IS THE ORDER

The vendor has the mode in the COMMON BLOCK:

    {0x0800, 0x03, 0x01, CSIPHY_DEFAULT_PARAMS},
    {0x0800, 0x02, 0x00, CSIPHY_2PH_REGS},     <- D-PHY
    {0x0800, 0x0E, 0x00, CSIPHY_3PH_REGS},     <- C-PHY

and in cam_csiphy_core.c it writes that WHOLE block before the while (lane_mask)
that applies the trios.

In my implementation the 0x0E was set by the C-PHY table itself, at the end of
each trio. The FINAL value matches, but the intermediate state does not: the PHY
spends the whole configuration of the first trio believing it is in D-PHY
(0x02), and only changes mode once it has thirty registers written.

This moves it to the vendor's place, where D-PHY sets its 0x02.
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c
@@ -1583,7 +1583,21 @@
 		writel_relaxed(0x03, csiphy->base +
 			       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
 		usleep_range(1000, 1200);
-		writel_relaxed(0x02, csiphy->base +
+		/*
+		 * The mode goes HERE, in the common block, and not at the end of the
+		 * lane table. The vendor has it this way:
+		 *
+		 *     {0x0800, 0x03, 0x01, CSIPHY_DEFAULT_PARAMS},
+		 *     {0x0800, 0x02, 0x00, CSIPHY_2PH_REGS},
+		 *     {0x0800, 0x0E, 0x00, CSIPHY_3PH_REGS},
+		 *
+		 * and writes the WHOLE common block before the while (lane_mask)
+		 * that applies the trios. Writing it afterwards -which is what
+		 * the C-PHY table did, with a 0x0E at the end of each trio- the
+		 * final value matches but the PHY goes through the whole configuration
+		 * of the first trio believing it is in D-PHY.
+		 */
+		writel_relaxed(cfg->cphy ? 0x0E : 0x02, csiphy->base +
 			       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
 	} else {
 		val = 0x00;
